id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I stumbled over this one as well. I think what it does is correct (though a bit weird):\r\n\r\nFirst, it gathers values into `char32_t` in a `String` (0-255) literally (as if it was `latin1`).\r\nThen, it checks whether it was actually utf-8. If yes, it converts the values back to `char` (through `ascii(true)`), and sends them into the `extend_utf8` to be re-interpreted as utf-8 as a `String`. \r\n\r\nThis is pretty wasteful, but making it use utf-8 immediately would require a small re-write of this section, which is out of scope for this PR.","created_at":"2025-03-27T13:56:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-27T13:58:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104556#discussion_r2016729968","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104556","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2016729968"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104556#discussion_r2016729968"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104556"}},"rea